-
-This work discusses four selected quantum attack models: Grover Search Attack (GSA), Quantum Chosen-Plaintext Attack (QCPA), Quantum Known-Plaintext Attack (QKPA), and Quantum State Tomography Attack. These attacks are selected deliberately rather than randomly, because they directly target the key-search complexity, the unitary encryption structure, the relationship between the $O$ and $C$ quantum images, and the recoverability of the encrypted quantum
