-T_{\rm classical}
-=
-O(2^{384}),
-$
-While the Grover-based quantum search complexity becomes
-\[
-T_{\rm Grover}
-=
-O(2^{384/2})
-=
-O(2^{192}).
-\]
-
-Since \(2^{192}\) is significantly larger than \(2^{128}\), the minimum quantum-security threshold, then the proposed QEF scheme provides a strong security margin against GSA. Consequently, the $K_{\rm total}$ meets the criterion \(L_{\rm total}\geq256\). Therefore, the proposed QEF retains its computational resistance against Grover-based quantum brute-force attacks.
